+# Add t and use it to check PlaceBlock arguments
+
+Adds the [t](https://github.com/osyrisrblx/t) runtime type checker as a package and switches the
+`PlaceBlock` remote handler to it. Remotes we add later can check their arguments the same way.
+
+## Changes
+
+- `pesde.toml`: adds `t = { wally = "osyrisrblx/t", version = "=3.1.1" }`. It installs from Wally
+  through pesde like our other packages, pinned exactly, and mounts at
+  `ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t`. 3.1.1 is the latest version in the Wally index.
+- `src/ServerScriptService/BlockPlacement.server.luau`: the hand-written `typeof` and NaN checks
+  become one t checker, `isPlaceBlockArgs = t.tuple(t.string, t.intersection(t.Vector3, isNotNaN))`.
+- `README.md`: adds t to the package table.
+
+## The handler still runs every check it ran before
+
+| Check | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| Block type name is a string | `typeof(blockTypeName) ~= "string"` | `t.string` |
+| Position is a Vector3 | `typeof(position) ~= "Vector3"` | `t.Vector3` |
+| Position has no NaN component | `position ~= position` | `isNotNaN`, the same comparison |
+| Block type exists | `BlockTypes.ByName` lookup | unchanged |
+| Rate limit, character present, cell above Y = 0 and free, within reach | as before | unchanged |
+
+`t.Vector3` only checks `typeof`. It does not look at the components (only `t.number` rejects NaN),
+so the NaN check stays as a custom checker in the intersection. The handler's parameters stay typed
+`unknown`. t's checkers don't narrow Luau types, so the two uses after the check cast
+(`blockTypeName :: string`, `position :: Vector3`).
+
+## Before testing
+
+`pesde.lock` is **not** updated in this PR. pesde wasn't run while this was written, so the
+package isn't installed yet. Until you install it, the script fails at
+`require(ReplicatedStorage.Packages.t)`. Run these from the repo root:
+
+1. Stop `rojo serve` if it is running. An install replaces `roblox_packages`, and Rojo 7.7.x can
+   crash when watched files disappear.
+2. `pesde install`
+3. Commit the updated `pesde.lock` to this branch.
+4. `rojo sourcemap default.project.json -o sourcemap.json --include-non-scripts`, so luau-lsp can
+   type the new package.
+5. Restart `rojo serve` and reconnect the Rojo plugin in Studio.
+
+## Not yet run
+
+pesde, Rojo, luau-lsp, selene, and StyLua couldn't run while this was written. After installing,
+run the checks from the README (`luau-lsp analyze`, `selene src`, `stylua --check src`), then
+playtest:
+
+- Placing each block type within reach still works.
+- Firing `PlaceBlock` with a non-string name, a non-Vector3 position,
+  `Vector3.new(0 / 0, 0, 0)`, an unknown block name, or a cell out of reach places nothing and
+  raises no error.
+
+🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
